---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import MermaidDiagram from '../components/MermaidDiagram.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Testing Strategy" sectionLabel="How It Works" activeSlug="testing">

<div class="panel-intro">
  <h2>Testing Strategy</h2>
  <p>
    VibeCrew provides testing commands for your project code <em>and</em> includes its own comprehensive
    test suite for the plugin's 127 bash scripts. This page covers both.
  </p>

  <div class="key-points">
    <div class="key-point">
      <span class="key-icon purple">&#9874;</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Project Testing</strong>
        4 slash commands for TDD, E2E, accessibility, and performance testing in your project.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="key-point">
      <span class="key-icon green">&#9939;</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Plugin Test Suite</strong>
        1413 unit tests + 69 integration tests validating VibeCrew's own scripts.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Testing Your Project -->
<section class="section">
  <h3>Testing Your Project</h3>
  <p>VibeCrew provides 4 testing commands that work on your project code. Each integrates with the Vibe Score &mdash; running these commands earns bonuses, skipping them incurs deductions.</p>

  <div class="agent-table-wrap">
    <table class="agent-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Tool</th><th>What It Does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>/tdd</code></td>
          <td>Vitest / Jest</td>
          <td>Red-green-refactor cycle. Writes ONE failing test, implements minimum code to pass, refactors, and commits. Produces a Discipline Score (0&ndash;10) measuring TDD adherence.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>/e2e</code></td>
          <td>Playwright</td>
          <td>Scaffolds Page Object Model, generates spec files with accessibility-first locators, and runs with trace-on-failure for debugging.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>/a11y</code></td>
          <td>axe-core</td>
          <td>WCAG 2.1 AA audit: automated axe scan, keyboard navigation checklist, ARIA validation. Saves a JSON report to the project.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>/perf-test</code></td>
          <td>k6</td>
          <td>Load, stress, spike, and soak test profiles. Configures thresholds and reports p95/p99 latency, throughput, and error rates.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="key-points">
    <div class="key-point">
      <span class="key-icon amber">&#9888;</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Project tests, not plugin tests</strong>
        <p>These commands test <em>your</em> application code. The section below covers VibeCrew's own internal test suite.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

  <h4 class="agent-table-heading">TDD Rationalization Resistance</h4>
  <p class="cmd-group-desc">
    The <code>/tdd</code> command includes built-in resistance to common reasons for skipping test-driven development. When the agent detects &ldquo;red flag&rdquo; phrases (like &ldquo;I&rsquo;ll add tests later&rdquo; or &ldquo;this is too simple to test&rdquo;), it stops and returns to the Red phase. The Iron Law: <strong>write code before the test? Delete it. Start over.</strong>
  </p>

<hr>

<!-- Plugin Test Suite -->
<section class="section">
  <h3>Plugin Test Suite</h3>
  <p>
    VibeCrew's 127 bash scripts form complex workflow chains. 1413 unit tests validate individual
    scripts in isolation. 69 integration tests validate the chains compose correctly &mdash; catching
    the category of bugs that only appear when script A's output becomes script B's input.
    All tests run in isolated temp directories with mocked external tools &mdash; zero network, zero side effects.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- Testing Flow -->
<h4 class="agent-table-heading">Testing Flow</h4>
<p class="cmd-group-desc">
  How tests flow through the system, from development to CI to regression feedback.
</p>

<MermaidDiagram chart={`flowchart TD
    DEV["Developer writes code"] --> UNIT["Unit Tests<br/>1413 tests · ~2min"]
    DEV --> INT["Integration Tests<br/>69 tests · ~2-5min"]
    UNIT --> CI["CI Pipeline<br/>ubuntu + macOS matrix"]
    INT --> CI
    CI --> PASS{"All pass?"}
    PASS -->|Yes| MERGE["Merge to main"]
    PASS -->|No| FIX["Fix failures"]
    FIX --> DEV
    MERGE --> WRAP["/wrap session"]
    WRAP --> DETECT["detect-fix-commits.sh<br/>Scan for fix: commits"]
    DETECT --> REGTEST{"Has test<br/>changes?"}
    REGTEST -->|No| SKELETON["generate-regression-test.sh<br/>Create test skeleton"]
    SKELETON --> SCORE["-5 Vibe Score"]
    REGTEST -->|Yes| OK["No deduction"]
    style UNIT fill:#bfb,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px
    style INT fill:#bbf,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px
    style CI fill:#ffd,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px
    style SKELETON fill:#fde8e8,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px
    style OK fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px`}
  caption="Full testing flow: unit and integration tests feed CI, /wrap detects fix commits without regression tests."
/>

<!-- Testing Pyramid -->
<h4 class="agent-table-heading">Testing Pyramid</h4>
<p class="cmd-group-desc">
  Two automated tiers plus manual validation for complete coverage.
</p>

<MermaidDiagram chart={`flowchart TD
    A["Manual Testing<br/>(Full Claude Code session)"] --> B
    B["Integration Tests<br/>(69 tests — workflow chains)"] --> C
    C["Unit Tests<br/>(1413 tests — individual scripts)"]
    style A fill:#f9f,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px
    style B fill:#bbf,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px
    style C fill:#bfb,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px`}
  caption="Test pyramid: unit tests form the base, integration tests validate chains, manual testing covers full sessions."
/>

<!-- Test Suites Table -->
<h4 class="agent-table-heading">Test Suites</h4>
<div class="agent-table-wrap">
  <table class="agent-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Suite</th><th>Tests</th><th>What It Tests</th><th>Speed</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Unit</strong></td>
        <td>1413</td>
        <td>Individual script logic, edge cases, error paths</td>
        <td>~2min</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Feature Lifecycle</strong></td>
        <td>16</td>
        <td>claim &rarr; 6 phases &rarr; done state machine (incl. complexity-aware skipping)</td>
        <td>~15s</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Session Startup</strong></td>
        <td>13</td>
        <td>Migration, sync, repair, model-change detection</td>
        <td>~10s</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Hook Enforcement</strong></td>
        <td>16</td>
        <td>Full PreToolUse &rarr; PostToolUse pipeline</td>
        <td>~10s</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Wrap Sequence</strong></td>
        <td>14</td>
        <td>Score &rarr; docs &rarr; sidebar &rarr; handoff &rarr; agent metrics</td>
        <td>~10s</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Concurrency</strong></td>
        <td>10</td>
        <td>Lock contention, parallel writers, stale cleanup</td>
        <td>~30s</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<!-- Test Isolation -->
<h4 class="agent-table-heading">How Tests Are Isolated</h4>
<p class="cmd-group-desc">
  Every test creates an ephemeral project directory, runs in isolation, and cleans up after itself.
</p>

<MermaidDiagram chart={`flowchart LR
    A["mktemp -d"] --> B["git init"]
    B --> C["Create .vibecrew/"]
    C --> D["Run test"]
    D --> E["rm -rf"]
    style A fill:#e8f4fd,stroke:#333
    style E fill:#fde8e8,stroke:#333`}
  caption="Test lifecycle: create temp dir, initialize git, create state files, run test, clean up."
/>

<!-- Mocking Strategy -->
<h4 class="agent-table-heading">Mocking Strategy</h4>
<p class="cmd-group-desc">
  External tools are always mocked. Internal scripts run for real in integration tests.
</p>

<div class="agent-table-wrap">
  <table class="agent-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Layer</th><th>What's Mocked</th><th>How</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>External CLIs</td>
        <td><code>gh</code>, <code>glab</code>, <code>node</code>, <code>npm</code></td>
        <td><code>mock_command()</code> &mdash; executable stub prepended to PATH</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Package managers</td>
        <td><code>bun</code>, <code>pnpm</code>, <code>yarn</code></td>
        <td>Same PATH prepend pattern</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>System tools</td>
        <td><code>terminal-notifier</code>, <code>timeout</code></td>
        <td>Same pattern</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>File system</td>
        <td>None &mdash; uses real temp dirs</td>
        <td><code>mktemp -d</code> with cleanup in teardown</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Git</td>
        <td>Real git in temp repos</td>
        <td><code>git init</code> in setup, real commits when needed</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Internal scripts</td>
        <td><strong>Not mocked</strong> in integration tests</td>
        <td>Scripts call each other directly</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<!-- Running Tests -->
<h4 class="agent-table-heading">Running Tests</h4>
<p class="cmd-group-desc">
  The test runner supports three modes via a single entry point.
</p>

<pre><code>tests/run-tests.sh              # All tests (unit + integration)
tests/run-tests.sh unit         # Unit tests only
tests/run-tests.sh integration  # Integration tests only</code></pre>

<!-- Regression Test Feedback Loop -->
<h4 class="agent-table-heading">Regression Test Feedback Loop</h4>
<p class="cmd-group-desc">
  When bug fixes are committed without accompanying tests, VibeCrew automatically generates
  regression test skeletons to close the loop.
</p>

<MermaidDiagram chart={`flowchart LR
    A["fix: commit<br/>detected"] --> B{"Has test<br/>changes?"}
    B -->|No| C["detect-fix-commits.sh"]
    C --> D["generate-regression-test.sh"]
    D --> E["Skeleton committed<br/>with skip marker"]
    B -->|Yes| F["No action needed"]
    style A fill:#fde8e8,stroke:#333
    style E fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#333
    style F fill:#e8fde8,stroke:#333`}
  caption="Fix commits without tests trigger automatic skeleton generation during /wrap."
/>

<p>
  The Vibe Score applies a <strong>-5 deduction</strong> per fix commit without a regression test.
  After 3+ sessions with uncovered fixes, the Performance Coach proposes a CLAUDE.md mutation
  enforcing TDD-style bug fixing.
</p>

<!-- CI Pipeline -->
<h4 class="agent-table-heading">CI Pipeline</h4>
<p class="cmd-group-desc">
  GitHub Actions runs two parallel jobs on push/PR to <code>main</code>.
</p>

<div class="agent-table-wrap">
  <table class="agent-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Job</th><th>Suite</th><th>Speed</th><th>Timeout</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>unit-tests</code></td>
        <td><code>tests/*.bats</code></td>
        <td>~30s</td>
        <td>Default</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>integration-tests</code></td>
        <td><code>tests/integration/*.bats</code></td>
        <td>~2-5min</td>
        <td>10min</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p>
  Both run on <code>ubuntu-latest</code> + <code>macos-latest</code> matrix with <code>fail-fast: false</code>.
</p>

</DocsLayout>
